      "watchSceneIndex": 3,
      "content": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heroBlock",
            "title": "Crash and Tortue Monopusher",
            "subtitle": "Shaping Movement"
          },
          {
            "type": "scrollMediasBlock",
            "text": "An aesthetic quest challenges Cartier to surpass itself, as the Maison merges form and function by creating extraordinary movements.",
            "medias": [
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/crash/scrollMediasBlock1.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": ""
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/crash/scrollMediasBlock2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "A new skeleton shape for a cult silhouette"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/crash/scrollMediasBlock3.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "142 components in the smallest possible space"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/crash/scrollMediasBlock4.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "An iconic combination of platinum with a ruby cabochon"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/crash/scrollMediasBlock5.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "An accentuated distortion down to the crown"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "scrollWatchBlock",
            "texts": [
              "For the Crash watch, a shaped movement is a true technical feat, adapted to the irregular case of this cult design. The moving parts of the movement become one with the bridges, shaped like Roman numerals for a time-telling function.",
              "The combination of the Maison’s signature metal platinum with a burgundy strap is a nod to the iconic ruby cabochon traditionally found on Cartier’s platinum watches."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "videoBlock",
            "media": {
              "url": "/videos/productPages/crash/videoBlock.mp4",
              "type": "video",
              "ariaLabel": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "productsBlock",
            "text": "The Tortue Monopusher Chronograph is fitted with the Manufacture 1928 MC movement, a single-button chronograph movement adjusted to fit the shape of the case. The movement is 4.30mm thick, making it the Maison's thinnest chronograph.",
            "medias": [
