    {
      "market": "France",
      "title": "Santos-Dumont and Tortue",
      "uri": "the-manufacture-between-innovation-and-tradition",
      "slug": "the-manufacture-between-innovation-and-tradition",
      "type": "product",
      "loaded": 1,
      "watchSceneIndex": 4,
      "content": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heroBlock",
            "title": "Santos-Dumont and Tortue",
            "subtitle": "The manufacture between tradition and innovation"
          },
          {
            "type": "scrollMediasBlock",
            "text": "At the Cartier watchmaking Manufacture in Switzerland, the fundamental approach brings together the latest technical advances with the importance of watchmaking heritage.",
            "medias": [
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock1.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": ""
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "A legacy of innovation and a pioneering spirit"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock3.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "The obsidian dial marks a feat of gem-cutting"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock4.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "Inspired by the flexibility of the first made-to-measure metal watch bracelets"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock5.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "True to the elegance and\n pioneering spirit of the original"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "scrollWatchBlock",
            "texts": [
              "For the Santos-Dumont collection, the pioneering spirit of Alberto Santos-Dumont inspires the reinvention of its bracelet: balancing a legacy of precious jewellery bracelets with the technical challenge of extreme flexibility.",
              "The metal bracelet flows with the elegance of 394 tiny links, entirely developed, built and assembled in the Manufacture."
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "videoBlock",
            "media": {
              "url": "/videos/productPages/santos-and-tortue/videoBlock.mp4",
              "type": "video",
              "ariaLabel": ""
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "productsBlock",
            "medias": [
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/productsBlock1.webp",
                "ariaLabel": ""
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/productsBlock2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "scrollMediasBlock",
            "text": "Within the Maison des Métiers d’Art, located just beside the watchmaking Manufacture, rare and ancestral crafts find new expressions. This Tortue watch demonstrates the beauty of champlevé enamelling to recreate the Panther.",
            "medias": [
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock1-2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": ""
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock2-2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "A masterful use of champlevé enamel"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock3-2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "130 hours of enamel work"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock4-2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "The Panther meets the Tortue watch"
              },
              {
                "url": "/images/productPages/santos-and-tortue/scrollMediasBlock5-2.webp",
                "ariaLabel": "",
                "subtitle": "Created in the Maison des Métiers d'Art"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "textBlock",
            "text": "Over 15 different tones were used in each piece, requiring more than 36 separate firings. It took 80 hours to enamel the dial and 50 hours to enamel the case."
          },
          {
            "type": "sliderBlock",
            "layoutVariant": "landscape",
